    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d92">

                <pb facs="0226" n="132" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg132"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">255.11 Diamond, Legs/14:Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Bremen</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Leonard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bremen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-09-08T12:00:00+01:00">September 8,
                        1930—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received September 8—9:35 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Supplementing telegram from Consul at Cologne,<anchor n="58" xml:id="d92-f1"/>
                    local police authorities inform me John Diamond expelled from Bremen, having
                    sailed from Hamburg Saturday afternoon 6th on freight steamer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hanover</hi>, scheduled to sail directly to Philadelphia
                    arriving there about 20th. He was held in police custody before sailing.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Leonard</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
